diff --git a/docs/internationalization.md b/docs/internationalization.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..39e37e4
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/internationalization.md
@@ -0,0 +1,38 @@
+# Languages
+
+Fizzy supports English (`en`, the default) and Japanese (`ja`). Open any page
+with `?locale=ja` or `?locale=en` to choose a language. Other values are ignored.
+An anonymous choice lasts for the session and is saved to the identity after
+successful authentication. An authenticated choice is saved immediately and
+applies across that identity's accounts and future sign-ins. Signing out clears
+the browser-session choice, not the identity's preference.
+
+Requests scope I18n with `with_locale`, including redirects and authentication.
+Mailers use the recipient identity at delivery time; an explicit anonymous
+choice can also be supplied for a magic-link email. Push notifications and
+HTML broadcasts use the receiver's locale, not the actor's. Fragment and
+collection caches include the locale. Turbo snapshots/offline caches are cleared
+when changing language.
+
+## Adding or changing copy
+
+* Add matching entries to `config/locales/en.yml` and `ja.yml`. Preserve existing
+  English wording, whitespace and interpolation. Translate complete messages
+  where possible; do not concatenate English grammar into a translated phrase.
+* Use Rails translation helpers for trusted `_html` entries; pass user content
+  as escaped interpolation values, never as translation keys or raw markup.
+* Keep identifiers, URLs, data attributes controlling behavior, and user-authored
+  content unchanged. System history is rendered from its recorded event.
+* Store keys, not translated strings, in constants so lookup happens per request.
+* Use `I18n.l` for displayed dates, not `strftime`. Keep machine timestamps and
+  URL date parameters in their existing formats. Browser dates use the document
+  locale, and browser copy comes from the `browser` catalog embedded in the head.
+* Framework date/time, plural, number and validation messages live in
+  `framework.*.yml`. Onboarding copy lives in `onboarding.*.yml`.
+* Static public error pages must include both languages with language attributes.
+* Lexxy's own JavaScript package strings are deliberately not translated here.
+
+Run `script/i18n/check` for locale persistence, catalog parity, date, validation,
+and email checks. `script/i18n/check --browser` additionally exercises real
+browser date formatting and language switching. Run `bin/rails test` for the
+English compatibility suite. Optional SaaS view copy uses the same catalogs.
